// lucid/_C/core/AmpPolicyTable.def
//
// The autocast policy of every op that has one, per device.  This is the
// only place an op's autocast behaviour is decided: ``SchemaGuard`` reads
// it for engine primitives, ``AmpScope`` for engine composites, and the
// Python layer through ``engine.amp_policy_for``.
//
//     LUCID_AMP_ROW(name, METAL, CPU)
//
// ``name`` is the op's schema name, or the composite's name.  The columns:
//
//   LOWER   cast floating inputs to the autocast dtype (CPU float16
//           computes in float32 — Accelerate has no float16 arithmetic)
//   FP32    cast floating inputs to float32
//   WIDEST  cast floating inputs to the widest floating dtype among them
//   KEEP    leave the inputs alone
//
// An op with no row keeps its inputs' dtype on both devices, which is also
// the reference framework's default; a KEEP column only appears beside a
// non-KEEP one.  The METAL column follows the reference framework's MPS
// list and the CPU column its CPU list.  Where the reference decomposes an
// op that Lucid runs as one (``square`` and ``cube`` into ``pow``,
// ``trace`` into ``sum``, ``cross_entropy_loss`` into ``log_softmax`` and
// ``nll_loss``), the row carries the decomposition's effective policy.
// Where Lucid builds a family of public ops from a few engine primitives,
// the rows name the primitives: ``fftn`` / ``ifftn`` / ``rfftn`` /
// ``irfftn`` cover every ``lucid.fft`` function (the reference lists each
// ``fft_*`` op, and every one decomposes into these four here).  WIDEST
// rows are applied across all of an op's floating operands by
// ``AmpScope::cast_widest``; ``scatter_add`` is the reference's
// ``scatter_add`` (the ``index_scatter`` schema is ``sort``'s backward).
//
// Departures from the reference, on purpose:
//
//   ctc_loss         FP32 on Metal too — the reference has no MPS kernel
//                    for it, and the CPU answer is the one it is compared
//                    against.
//   pad              No row.  The reference's CPU list runs reflect and
//                    replicate padding in float32 and leaves constant and
//                    circular padding alone; Lucid's one ``pad`` schema takes
//                    the mode as an argument, so a row cannot tell them
//                    apart.  Reflect / replicate padding keeps a bfloat16
//                    input under a CPU autocast (a strict xfail in the test).
//   vdot             No row, as in the reference, but ``lucid.vdot`` is
//                    built on ``dot`` and so takes ``dot_1d``'s WIDEST row:
//                    on Metal it runs a float16 / float32 pair in float32
//                    where the reference refuses the pair.
//
// ``lstm_cell`` is ``nn.LSTMCell``'s step, applied at its entry.
//
// Rows are sorted by name, each name once — ``AmpPolicy.cpp`` refuses to
// compile otherwise.  ``lucid/test/unit/amp/test_autocast_policy_table.py``
// checks that every name is an op Lucid has.

LUCID_AMP_ROW(adaptive_avg_pool3d,          KEEP,   FP32)
LUCID_AMP_ROW(adaptive_max_pool3d,          KEEP,   FP32)
LUCID_AMP_ROW(addbmm,                       LOWER,  LOWER)
LUCID_AMP_ROW(addcdiv,                      WIDEST, KEEP)
LUCID_AMP_ROW(addcmul,                      WIDEST, KEEP)
LUCID_AMP_ROW(addmm,                        LOWER,  LOWER)
LUCID_AMP_ROW(addmv,                        LOWER,  KEEP)
LUCID_AMP_ROW(addr,                         LOWER,  KEEP)
LUCID_AMP_ROW(affine_grid,                  LOWER,  LOWER)
LUCID_AMP_ROW(arccos,                       FP32,   KEEP)
LUCID_AMP_ROW(arcsin,                       FP32,   KEEP)
